{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Negotiating a Warranty Section in Software Contracts "}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use when talking about the warranty section in a software contract. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about people's backgrounds in spoken or written documents.  Define strategies to make terms of reference and supplier assessment processes in technology acquisition, based on established protocols. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of a range of grammar and vocabulary, and with the appropriate level of formality and purpose, coherence and cohesion for the context.  Exchanges simple information on IT contracts and knowledge transfer, simulated processes of IT contracting, and technological negotiation."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Be Supposed To in Present and Past Statements"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Be supposed to</span> in present and past statements is used when you want to talk about things that were or are expected to happen."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You're supposed to warrant my software contract."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Be supposed to</span> is used when you want to talk about things that were arranged to happen, or are/were considered to be a certain way. <br/><br/>  Do not forget that a verb must be included following the structure <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span>; the verb presents the action that is/was expected to happen. <br/><br/>  This is the present tense structure: <br/><br/> Subject + <span class=\"strong\">Be+ Supposed to + Verb</span> + Complement <br/><br/> Example: <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">am supposed to sign</span> the software contract. </span> <br/><br/> And this is the past tense structure:<br/><br/> Subject + <span class=\"strong\">Was/ Were+ Supposed to + Verb </span>+ Complement <br/><br/> Example: <span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">was supposed to go</span> over the contract immediately. </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "It's supposed to show what the software will or won't do. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "It was supposed to be like that."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I think we were supposed to analyze these questions in advance."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Make Comparisons With As\u2026 As"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " If we want to establish <span class=\"strong\">comparisons</span> between two elements, we can use the structure <span class=\"strong\">as... as</span>."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It has to be analyzed as carefully as possible."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">As\u2026as</span>  is used to make <span class=\"strong\">comparisons</span> of equality. The sentences must have an <span class=\"strong\">adjective</span> or <span class=\"strong\">adverb</span> after the first <span class=\"strong\">as</span>. This means that both elements have to be <span class=\"italic\">equally clear.</span> <br/><br/>Example: <span class=\"italic\">The contract has to be <span class=\"strong\"> as clear as </span>  the agreement. </span> <br/><br/> If we use a noun phrase, we need to include <span class=\"strong\">much</span> or <span class=\"strong\">many</span>, depending on the noun we will mention afterwards. <br/><br/> Example: <span class=\"italic\">It needs to include <span class=\"strong\">as many details as</span> possible. </span></br></br>On the other hand, if we want to compare two objects by pointing out that one of them does not possess a characteristic in the same degree as the other one, we can use <span class=\"strong\">not as </span>. </br></br>Example: <span class=\"italic\">This software is <span class=\"strong\">not as useful as</span> the one you bought.</span> "}, {"type": "example", "content": "They told me it would help me as much as I needed. "}, {"type": "example", "content": " Every question on the checklist is as important as the others."}, {"type": "example", "content": "All the provisions should be as clear as possible."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "upset "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be angry or sad "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I'm really upset because you're supposed to warrant my software contract."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob08aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "detrimental "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that causes loss or negative consequences "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The warranty is supposed to help you avoid detrimental effects."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob08aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "contract "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a written agreement between two or more people  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  So, the warranty of my contract is supposed to have a time period. Right?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob08aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "must "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "modal verb that indicates an obligation or something that is required "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Besides, the provider must have the equipment to offer the services and therefore the services are supposed to be performed in a workmanlike manner."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob08aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "workmanlike "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something or someone efficient when performing a specific job or activity "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Besides, the provider must have the equipment to offer the services and therefore the services are supposed to be performed in a workmanlike manner."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob08aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "checklist "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "list of activities or goals to be achieved "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  What's a checklist of provisions that should be negotiated in the section?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob08aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for more information about a warranty section in a software contract of a laptop."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Design an example of a warranty section to be included in a software contract."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Include the typical provisions in a warranty section."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your work with your classmates."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research about what a warranty section is."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I create a warranty section for a laptop software contract."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I integrate the important parts of a warranty section in a self-created one"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I show my work to classmates and discuss ideas with them. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "video", "template_override": 1, "id": 3, "contents": [{"value": {"video_src": "enpe8n7le02ob08re2vid01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": "<strong>Jim: </strong> I'm really upset because you're supposed to warrant my software contract.<br>"}, {"time": "4000", "image": "", "id": 1, "text": "<strong>Claire: </strong> It was like that. We are aware of the importance of the warranty. It's supposed to show what the software will or won't do. <br>"}, {"time": "10500", "image": "", "id": 2, "text": "<strong>Jim: </strong> The performance of the software is specified in this warranty. <br>"}, {"time": "13500", "image": "", "id": 3, "text": "<strong>Claire: </strong> That's why it has to be analyzed as carefully as possible because it shows the factors that can affect the software. The warranty is supposed to help you avoid detrimental effects. <br>"}, {"time": "23000", "image": "", "id": 4, "text": "<strong>Jim: </strong> Exactly. It was supposed to be like that. They told me the warranty would help me as much as I needed, but I've had many difficulties. <br>"}, {"time": "30500", "image": "", "id": 5, "text": "<strong>Claire: </strong> The best way to review the warranty section is by putting it into action, and the way to negotiate the contract is by asking some questions: First, what are the licensor's responsibilities in the warranty section? Second, what are the licensee's responsibilities? Third, what's a checklist of provisions that should be negotiated in the section? And finally, what's the general checklist of provisions that is supposed to be included? Every question on the checklist is as important as the others. <br>"}, {"time": "59000", "image": "", "id": 6, "text": "<strong>Jim: </strong> I think we were supposed to analyze these questions in advance. What are those provisions that are included? <br>"}, {"time": "65000", "image": "", "id": 7, "text": "<strong>Claire: </strong> For instance, the licensor is supposed to certify that the software corresponds to the Functional Specifications. Besides, the provider must have the equipment to offer the services; therefore, the services are supposed to be performed in a workmanlike manner. The software also has to comply with all the laws and the software warranty must have a period. All the provisions should be as clear as possible. <br>"}, {"time": "89000", "image": "", "id": 8, "text": "<strong>Jim: </strong>  So, the warranty for my contract is supposed to have a time period, right? <br>"}, {"time": "93500", "image": "", "id": 9, "text": "<strong>Claire: </strong> Actually, it includes it and it expired two months ago. <br>"}]}, "type": "video"}]}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about the importance of the warranty section in a software contract. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can list some questions to be asked when negotiating the warranty section in a software contract. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can discuss some provisions to include in a typical warranty section. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What's a software contract?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Is it mandatory to have a software contact? Why? Why not?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"